{"id": "evt-0001", "org_id": "acme", "kind": "slack_message", "ts": "2026-09-18T10:00:00Z", "actor": "arjun", "channel": "eng-backend", "thread_id": "slack:eng-backend:1758172800", "text": "Postgres row locks on sessions are killing p99 during checkout peaks. We are seeing >80ms latency.", "refs": {"service_ids": ["session-store"], "decision_id": "DEC-017", "ticket_id": null, "doc_id": null, "pr_id": null}, "supersedes": null, "reverses": null, "facts": [{"subject": "session-store", "predicate": "EXPERIENCING", "object": "latency-spikes", "valid_at": "2026-09-18T10:00:00Z", "invalid_at": null}]}
{"id": "evt-0002", "org_id": "acme", "kind": "slack_message", "ts": "2026-09-18T10:05:00Z", "actor": "priya", "channel": "eng-backend", "thread_id": "slack:eng-backend:1758172800", "text": "Postgres gives us ACID guarantees. If we lose session tokens mid-checkout, payments will fail unpredictably.", "refs": {"service_ids": ["session-store"], "decision_id": "DEC-017", "ticket_id": null, "doc_id": null, "pr_id": null}, "supersedes": null, "reverses": null, "facts": [{"subject": "session-store", "predicate": "REQUIRES", "object": "ACID-guarantees", "valid_at": "2026-09-18T10:05:00Z", "invalid_at": null}]}
{"id": "evt-0003", "org_id": "acme", "kind": "slack_message", "ts": "2026-09-18T10:12:00Z", "actor": "arjun", "channel": "eng-backend", "thread_id": "slack:eng-backend:1758172800", "text": "Redis cluster with volatile-lru TTL cuts lookup times to <5ms. Most auth tokens are ephemeral anyway.", "refs": {"service_ids": ["session-store"], "decision_id": "DEC-017", "ticket_id": null, "doc_id": null, "pr_id": null}, "supersedes": null, "reverses": null, "facts": [{"subject": "session-store", "predicate": "STORED_IN", "object": "Redis", "valid_at": "2026-09-18T10:12:00Z", "invalid_at": null}]}
{"id": "evt-0004", "org_id": "acme", "kind": "slack_message", "ts": "2026-09-18T10:18:00Z", "actor": "meera", "channel": "eng-backend", "thread_id": "slack:eng-backend:1758172800", "text": "From SRE side, make sure memory alerts and replica failovers are properly configured if we go Redis.", "refs": {"service_ids": ["session-store"], "decision_id": "DEC-017", "ticket_id": null, "doc_id": null, "pr_id": null}, "supersedes": null, "reverses": null, "facts": [{"subject": "session-store", "predicate": "MONITORED_BY", "object": "sre", "valid_at": "2026-09-18T10:18:00Z", "invalid_at": null}]}
{"id": "evt-0005", "org_id": "acme", "kind": "slack_message", "ts": "2026-09-18T10:25:00Z", "actor": "priya", "channel": "eng-backend", "thread_id": "slack:eng-backend:1758172800", "text": "Fine, let us trial Redis with a fallback mechanism and document the architecture decision.", "refs": {"service_ids": ["session-store"], "decision_id": "DEC-017", "ticket_id": null, "doc_id": null, "pr_id": null}, "supersedes": null, "reverses": null, "facts": [{"subject": "session-store", "predicate": "AGREED_ON", "object": "Redis-trial", "valid_at": "2026-09-18T10:25:00Z", "invalid_at": null}]}
{"id": "evt-0006", "org_id": "acme", "kind": "slack_message", "ts": "2026-09-18T10:30:00Z", "actor": "arjun", "channel": "eng-backend", "thread_id": "slack:eng-backend:1758172800", "text": "Decision: move sessions to Redis. I will open Linear ticket LIN-391 and write ADR-038.", "refs": {"service_ids": ["session-store"], "decision_id": "DEC-017", "ticket_id": null, "doc_id": null, "pr_id": null}, "supersedes": null, "reverses": null, "facts": [{"subject": "session-store", "predicate": "STORED_IN", "object": "Redis", "valid_at": "2026-09-18T10:30:00Z", "invalid_at": null}]}
